{
  "sourcePatchId": "35a07e2c-4b00-40ec-b71f-d361476ec81e",
  "name": "HSB Mono",
  "description": "Monophonic hsboscil synth with five sine-wave octaves and independent cyclic tonality/brightness. Last-note priority; overlapping/touching notes share an envelope. Patch-local portk memory glides across gaps up to approximately 20 ms; longer gaps start directly at the new pitch. A positive gap retriggers the amplitude envelope, as in a slide bass; it does not extend the phrase gate. Legato half-time defaults to 60 ms (higher = slower). Velocity-sensitive, 6 ms attack / 150 ms decay / 0.8 sustain / 80 ms release. Suggested MIDI range 36-84. Performance controls: Tonality 0-1 octave cycle, Brightness -2 to +2 octaves, Legato half-time 1-500 ms. MIDI control channel defaults to 16; CC20 Tonality, CC74 Brightness, CC5 Legato half-time. CC0 recalls the performance setting; CC1 minimum, CC127 maximum, with 10 ms smoothing. Rack controls are read at phrase start. CCs affect held notes; notes never reset controllers. Instances sharing a control channel share CC automation, but their voice/glide state remains separate. Route Stereo Output through the mixer to Master.",
